{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact head 06e211c204c14a53a8afe7dba486244f7cf855c8.\n\nTwo blockers:\n\n1. docs/reference/mcp/state.md says that a report with status instead of verdict, an approval without an artifact, and a citation naming no event are all effective and move the commitment. The third claim is not generally true: an unresolved citation may occur on a non-commitment act, and if it is the only claimed basis it can make a basis-constrained act ineffective. Describe only the narrower guarantee: the record lands, while projected.verdict/reason and unresolved_rests_on explain how it was read.\n\n2. The exact carry commit 06e211c is a substantive conflict-resolution commit but carries no Rests-On trailer. Its implementation and both exact-head artifacts are based on Claude's old self-request chain rather than the motivating ratified decision required by current AGENTS.md for self-initiated work. Re-cut the exact head under a valid current basis, add the required trailer, and re-anchor both artifacts. Any ratifier decision that explicitly grandfathers the old chain may resolve the basis issue, but this head does not contain or cite one.\n\nThe implementation itself is coherent: one post-append snapshot supplies the undefined-kind warning and all projection notes; decisions correctly resolve statement-free ratify/supersede records; refused reviews preserve the submitted verdict and surface the fold reason; all verbs expose projection unavailability. The one-snapshot conflict resolution is the simpler safe choice; a second residentclient helper call would duplicate a potentially cold fold. The bounded number of references makes the linear decision scans acceptable here.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are the Workroom application interpreter/projection, MCP surface, and its reference documentation. The semantic-free kernel and durable/projection contracts are preserved; no architecture-page change is needed. Security: the act is still appended